      <h1>About Me</h1>

      <p>
        I'm James — a systems architect, DevOps engineer, and lifelong tinkerer.
        I build secure, predictable environments and love turning complex problems
        into clean, automated solutions. Whether I'm designing infrastructure,
        optimizing workflows, or experimenting with new ideas, I approach every
        project with curiosity and pride.
      </p>

      <p>
        My background spans infrastructure modernization, automation, security,
        and cross-team enablement. I’ve led initiatives that stabilized systems,
        improved developer experience, and strengthened operational hygiene.
        I’m at my best when I’m building something that blends reliability with
        creativity.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside of the professional work, I love experimenting — building small
        tools, interactive demos, and playful projects that teach real concepts
        in fun ways. That’s why I created the “For Fun” section of this site:
        a place to explore ideas, test new technologies, and share the joy of
        building things just because they’re interesting.
      </p>

      <p>
        JTCodeForge is my workshop — a place where professional engineering and
        creative experimentation meet. Thanks for stopping by.
      </p>
    </main>
